One more: screenshots. I'll run start.sh (which runs node default-start.mjs) → starts server on port 3000 (or PORT). Then open playwright, screenshot. Need to interact to start audio? For screenshot visual, the begin overlay will show. I can click to start then screenshot. But audio not needed for screenshot. Actually the game renders canvas even before begin? I'll render the scene behind overlay always (so screenshot shows game). The overlay just dims. On first interaction hide overlay and start audio. But ripples/orb need pointer; auto-drift orb works. Let me auto-drift orb from start so scene is alive. Overlay is semi-transparent with "enter" button. Screenshot will show overlay + scene. That's fine. But for verifying game, I'll click begin via playwright then screenshot.

